# fixedbugs, defect 2572: the header a group names is found first beside the
# program as a link to a device, `/dev/null` (made in the case's copy,
# `links`). A link to a device there was read by clang as an empty header
# and told *`x.h` declares no `x_one`*, and a FIFO there hung `heroes build`
# in clang's first listing until it was killed: the search is now walked
# before any clang starts, and the group is refused with what stands there.
# A FIFO cannot be tracked by git, so the compiler's own tests hold that one
# (`cli/header_stands.hero`, `module/reading.hero`).

extern "x.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function x_one() -> i32

function main()
    print(x_one().to_str())
